<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="016" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>B-3 decision lookup search and REST route</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>after 013</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api and authorization; new service and endpoint (.cs)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security boundary (authorization tag): the server must stop a client widening a search (plan-driven entity, D-18 matter scoping, caller record access, fail closed)</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns IDecisionLookupSearch.cs, DecisionLookupSearch.cs, SignalsModule.cs and DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs in its wave; 014 and 021 touch none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>013</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, endpoints, authorization, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add IDecisionLookupSearch, a plan-driven workforce lookup that searches contacts, matter-scoped budgets and organisations as the caller, and expose it at GET /api/v1/signals/{signalId}/lookup?parameterCode=&amp;query= in the existing decision-plan route group, failing closed and never using the external-plane policy.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in secure server-side query construction over Dataverse OData and ASP.NET Core authorization.</role>
  <goal>IDecisionLookupSearch and DecisionLookupSearch exist and are registered; the REST route returns capped, scoped results for every lookup parameter of the six action types; the negatives in FR-07 hold.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-07, design §8 B-3: D-18 ('a budget belongs to the matter') is enforced today only by the Console's browser picker (Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/worklistLookup.ts:54-74; DecisionActionExecutors.cs:380-381). The external SPA's /fetch (ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs, guard L897, scope injection L301-356) shows the server-built, scoped, fail-closed pattern on the external plane; copy the pattern, not the plane. The Console keeps its browser picker in v1 (spec Assumptions).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/IDecisionLookupSearch.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionLookupSearch.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SignalsModule.cs (AddScoped IDecisionLookupSearch)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs (new group.MapGet("/{signalId:guid}/lookup") in the existing /api/v1/signals group)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Signals/DecisionLookupSearchTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Signals/DecisionLookupRouteAuthTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/DecisionLookupRouteContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs (guard L897, scope injection L301-356): pattern only</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionParameterSources.cs (plan parameter sources)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionActionExecutors.cs:380-381 (budget belongs to the matter)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/worklistLookup.ts:54-74 (current client-side rule)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">IDecisionCapability.GetPlanAsync supplies the plan that drives the lookup</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">The lookup entity and scoping rule come only from the Signal's decision plan for the given parameterCode; the client supplies only signalId, parameterCode and query text, and cannot name an entity, column or filter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every lookup read runs as the caller through IDataverseUserClient (OBO); no app-only read returns lookup results; an unpopulated ICallerContext returns UserContextRequired.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">No endpoint or MCP tool added or changed by this task carries the ExternalCollaboration policy or the external access guard; workforce routes use .RequireAuthorization() on the default workforce scheme plus existing policies.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The query text is escaped as an OData string literal before use; no user text is concatenated into a filter unescaped; results are capped at 25 per call.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Fail closed: an unreadable Signal returns the same uniform refusal the plan route returns; an unknown parameterCode returns ontology.decision.invalid_parameter; a Dataverse fault returns a failure, never a partial or unscoped list.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The route lives in the existing /api/v1/signals group in DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs (so EndpointMappingExtensions.cs is not edited) and inherits that group's authorization.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Every log statement or telemetry property this task adds records identifiers, sizes, timings and outcome/reason codes only: no bearer token, claim value, record text or tool argument (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every PR from this task that touches Services/Signals/**, Api/Signals/** or the worklist route is reviewed by spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 before merge (project CLAUDE.md §4); run /conflict-check before opening it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

