  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs (L301-356, L897) for the scoped-query pattern and DecisionParameterSources for how the plan declares lookup parameters.</step>
    <step order="2">Define IDecisionLookupSearch.SearchAsync(signalId, parameterCode, query, ct) and implement: load the plan as the caller; resolve the parameter's LookupEntity and scope (budget → filtered to the Signal's matter; contact; organisation); build the OData query server-side with the escaped query text; read as the caller; cap at 25.</step>
    <step order="3">Register it in SignalsModule.cs and map GET /{signalId:guid}/lookup in DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs, returning results or DecisionResultMapper.ToHttp failures.</step>
    <step order="4">Write unit tests per action type (revise-budget, reassign, add-todo, assign-work, assign-task, inquiry outside firm) and the negatives; write auth and contract tests for the route.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the Signals suites and ArchTests (RouteAuthorizationGuardTests must cover the new route); measure the publish-size delta; open the PR for ontology review.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If an action type's lookup parameter has no scoping rule in the plan that the server can apply, STOP and list it rather than inventing a rule.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the route would need any policy beyond the plan route group's existing authorization, STOP and escalate (auth diff; unified-access-control-r2 reviews).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Console browser lookup Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/worklistLookup.ts (Xrm.WebApi); external-plane ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs POST /api/v1/external/api/dataverse/fetch.</existing>
    <extension>No: a browser Xrm helper cannot run on the server, and the external route's dual-scheme policy and external access guard must not serve workforce callers.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Six action types (revise-budget, reassign, add-todo, assign-work, assign-task, inquiry outside firm) cannot be completed outside the Console, and D-18 stays enforced only in the browser.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/IDecisionLookupSearch.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionLookupSearch.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Signals/DecisionLookupSearchTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Signals/DecisionLookupRouteAuthTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/DecisionLookupRouteContractTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For each lookup parameter of the six action types, the search returns contacts, budgets of the Signal's matter, or organisations as the plan declares, at most 25 per call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a parameterCode not in the plan returns ontology.decision.invalid_parameter (REST: the mapped ProblemDetails).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a budget belonging to another matter never appears, even when the query text matches it exactly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a record the caller cannot read never appears (as-caller read; test with a caller lacking read on a seeded record).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a Signal the caller cannot read returns the same refusal as the decision-plan route; an anonymous call returns 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: query text containing a single quote or OData operators does not error and does not widen the result set.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The route's endpoint metadata carries no ExternalCollaboration policy (test) and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE) and the ontology review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>The 25-result cap and the route path /api/v1/signals/{signalId}/lookup are this task's concrete choices for 'capped' and 'a REST route' in FR-07; record them in notes/decisions.md. A seeding proof is requested for the other-matter-budget negative (a widened search is a data-exposure outcome).</notes>

